      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MR. TEDDY BEAR (1) turned in a plain run last time when eighth at Sandown over 515m behind Mepunga Zircon (30.09) in a Grade 5. Goes well out of this box with a win and five minor placings. Has winning claims on his best figures. PEPPER PIE (7) comes off an average effort last start when seventh at Sandown over 595m behind Lush Hour (35.27) in a Grade 4/5. Form from her last run is proving strong. Leading chance. ZIPPING UNA (4) is a talented type and proved too classy last time to win by 7 lengths at this track in a handy 23.02 beating Paw Cheyenne. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings five times from eight attempts. Sure to measure up. BILLY RAY MIKADO (6) racing over this distance brings the best out in him.",
